# ── What is NOT compared, and why (K-629) ────────────────────────────────────
#
# SCAN_ROOTS leaves the Rails skeleton out. These are the paths that exist in two
# or more demos and that nothing above compares; each line says what the copies
# are allowed to differ by.
#
# HONEST SCOPE, twice over.
#
# (1) These entries are DOCUMENTARY. Only their staleness is checked — a declared
#     path that no longer exists in two demos is an error — not their
#     completeness: proving no OTHER skeleton path is duplicated would mean
#     walking a demo tree full of gitignored local scratch, and filtering that
#     needs `git ls-files`, an external process in a check that runs on a bare
#     checkout with nothing but stdlib. The scan roots keep their undeclared-copy
#     guard; the skeleton has a record instead.
#
# (2) "Not compared" is not "not covered". config/routes.rb and
#     config/initializers/kiosk.rb ARE asserted by the rules at the bottom of
#     this file; db/schema.rb is the output of migrations this check compares
#     byte-for-byte; and every demo's whole skeleton is exercised by that demo's
#     CI job, which boots the app.
#
# One recurring shape, stated once instead of forty times: kiosk-demo-prove is a
# smaller, API-only Rails app generated on its own, so on a whole family of
# generator-output paths the seven operator demos agree byte-for-byte and prove
# alone differs. Where a reason below says "prove differs", that is what it means.
